    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">the KV cache for a given sequence is spread across multiple non-contiguous pages</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">the KVCache may become large since its size is proportional to the model size and the number of generated tokens.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">interact with all preceding KV cache and KV cache of themselves</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">KV-cache read amplification is a non-issue for modern architectures chunks as small as 40 tokens</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">reduce the overhead of loading the KV-cache without sacrificing model accuracy</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">the KV cache for a given sequence is spread across multiple non-contiguous pages.</hasEvidenceText>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/S0/R1#sparsification">
