    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2502.21231_rag::chunk_003</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">it is able to greatly reduce the disk I/O and PCIe bandwidth utilization compared to the baseline, replacing it with NVLink communication instead.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">requires only the exchange of activations between consecutive stages via peer-to-peer (P2P) communication</hasEvidenceText>
